    "context_description": "Chris Pappas maintains a commanding lead in the New Hampshire Democratic Senate primary due to his established record as a four-term U.S. representative, broad endorsements from party leaders including former Vice President Kamala Harris and retiring Sen. Jeanne Shaheen, and a substantial fundraising edge exceeding $15 million compared to challenger Karishma Manzur's roughly $415,000. Recent University of New Hampshire and Saint Anselm College polls show Pappas ahead by double digits among likely Democratic primary voters, though Manzur has narrowed the gap somewhat by consolidating support among younger and progressive voters on issues like campaign finance and foreign policy. With the September 8 primary just days away, trader consensus at 97.8% for Pappas reflects these structural advantages and limited time for a late reversal, while scenarios that could still shift outcomes include unusually high turnout among Manzur's base or unexpected late developments in voter sentiment.",
